{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc | sed -n '94,141p'; rg -n 'wait-set|pending|:park|call-effect|seq|epoch|variant|authorized|abandon|fork|durab' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc | sed -n '1,20p'; rg -n 'defn (put-request|call|append|next)|id-key' src/cljc/dao/stream/apply.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"    94\t;; Primitive operations\n    95\t;; Arithmetic and comparison ops are direct clojure.core references.\n    96\t;; Wrapped in (fn ...) only where VM semantics require it:\n    97\t;; - rest: clojure.core/rest returns a lazy seq; wrapped to return a vector\n    98\t;;   so that conj appends rather than prepends.\n    99\t;; - yin/def, require: return effect descriptors consumed by the engine.\n   100\t(def primitives\n   101\t  {'+ +,\n   102\t   '- -,\n   103\t   '* *,\n   104\t   '/ /,\n   105\t   '= =,\n   106\t   '== =,\n   107\t   '!= not=,\n   108\t   '< <,\n   109\t   '> >,\n   110\t   '<= <=,\n   111\t   '>= >=,\n   112\t   'not not,\n   113\t   'nil? nil?,\n   114\t   'empty? empty?,\n   115\t   'first first,\n   116\t   'rest (fn [a] (vec (rest a))), ; clojure.core/rest returns a lazy seq;\n   117\t   ;; vec coerces to vector so conj appends rather than prepends\n   118\t   'conj conj,\n   119\t   'assoc assoc,\n   120\t   'get get,\n   121\t   'vec vec,\n   122\t   'bytes->str #?(:clj (fn\n   123\t                         ([b] (String. ^bytes b \"UTF-8\"))\n   124\t                         ([b enc] (String. ^bytes b ^String enc)))\n   125\t                  :cljs (fn [b] (.apply js/String.fromCharCode nil b))\n   126\t                  :cljd (fn [b] (dart:core/String.fromCharCodes b))),\n   127\t   ;; Definition primitive - returns an effect\n   128\t   'yin/def (fn [k v] {:effect :vm/store-put, :key k, :val v}),\n   129\t   ;; Module loading primitive - returns an effect dispatched to the host\n   130\t   'require (fn [spec]\n   131\t              (let [ns-sym (if (vector? spec) (first spec) spec)]\n   132\t                {:effect :module/require, :module ns-sym}))})\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t(def call-in-stream-key\n   136\t  \"Store key for the shared apply inbound request stream (caller writes, callee reads).\"\n   137\t  :yin/call-in)\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(def call-out-stream-key\n   141\t  \"Store key for the shared apply outbound response stream (callee writes, caller reads).\"\n8:To safely \"lift on park\" and \"lower on resume\" across heterogeneous boundaries without violating host isolation or concurrency invariants, the following contracts must be fully specified before this feature is accepted:\n13:4. **Ownership Arbitration:** Emitting a continuation does not transfer ownership. Exclusion requires a **grounded authority** — a resource the grantor's boundary actually possesses, named in the value, independent of carriers — plus an **exporting state** that fences the source before publication, and **effect fencing** with authority epochs and stable operation ids, because absence of a lapse record is never evidence of tenure.\n40:wait entry or a `:parked-continuation` record is `{segment pc env stack k}`\n57:Three consequences are load-bearing. First, **a UCF value is content**: it has\n102: :yin.k/policy      :yin.k/exclusive}          ; §7.7  or :yin.k/fork\n228:sequences, and compiler-renamed artifacts address **differently**. The\n257:  `check-wait-set`'s round order, `semantic-restore`.\n342:under the emitter's attribution, and carried unchanged by every authorized\n343:snapshot variant and every retry of the same park (§7.7.2). A re-emission\n366:| explicit park | `:park` | `pc+1` | St at park | the resume value |\n390: :yin.k/reason   :next                     ; :park | :next | :put | :ffi | :ffi-request | :call-effect\n397: :yin.k/pending  {…}}                      ; the wait it was in, §7.4.3 — one variant per reason\n453:  *contains